{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Zebulun shall dwell by the shore of the sea.</b> He would go out to trade to Tyre and Sidon, to distant lands; therefore Moses prayed for him that he would succeed in his trade." "<b>And Issachar, in your tents.</b> His land was fit for sowing, and he would sit in his tents to guard his fields. And Moses prayed for him that he would rejoice in his fields. And likewise Jacob said to him: 'couching between the borders' — couching between the boundaries, to guard his fields."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:00.046202291Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}